course: dictionary
lesson: 14598
title: Plushy: cuddly toys and fancy things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plushy has two jobs, and the words around it show which one it is. As a noun, a plushy is a soft, cuddly toy, usually spelled plushie. «Mia won three plushies at the fair.» Mia won toys, so plushies names things you can hug.
explain: As an adjective, plushy describes something rich, soft and comfortable-looking, like plush fabric. «The plushy seats at the cinema were soft and grand.» Plushy means luxurious: fancy and expensive, sometimes a bit too much.
explain: To tell which one it is, look at what the word does in the sentence. If it names a thing you can cuddle, it is the noun. If it describes a seat, a carpet or a room, it is the adjective. Then swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Plushy is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
fact: As a noun, «plushy» means a soft, cuddly toy; the spelling «plushie» is the more usual one.
fact: As an adjective, «plushy» means rich and comfortable-looking, like plush.
fact: «Plushy» can mean luxurious, but it can also suggest that something is a bit too fancy.
fact: The adjective changes like this: plushy, plushier, plushiest.
exercise: «Mia won three plushies at the fair.» What does plushies mean here? | *Soft, cuddly toys | Small coins | Thick winter coats | Heavy wooden chairs
exercise: «The hotel lobby was plushy, with thick velvet sofas and gold lamps.» What does plushy mean? | Wet and muddy | Very small | Cold and empty | *Rich and luxurious
exercise: Ruby says her bed is covered with plushies. Is plushies a noun or an adjective here, and what does it mean? | *A noun: soft, cuddly toys | A noun: a fancy bed | An adjective: very small | An adjective: rich and soft
test: «The plushy blanket made the old sofa look cosy and grand.» What does plushy mean here? | Very noisy | *Rich and soft-looking, like plush | Cold and hard | Broken and dirty
test: Ruby hugged her favourite plushie all night. What is a plushie? | A noisy bird | A type of plush carpet | *A soft, cuddly toy | A fancy hotel room
exam: Which sentence uses plushy as an adjective? | Dad bought three plushies for the shop | She hugged a plushie in bed | *The plushy seats at the cinema were soft and grand | Sam carried his plushy everywhere
